{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508356-have-you-ever-portrayed-sybil-in-your-games","id":1508356,"title":"Have you ever portrayed Sybil in your games?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-14T07:38:15-07:00","id":1508356,"title":"Have you ever portrayed Sybil in your games?","content":"Hello everyone, I'd like to discuss something here regarding Sybil. We've never had much information about her, save that she's the only &quot;known&quot; female embraced by the &quot;father of the Abyss&quot; (i.e. The Lasombra Antediluvian). Have you ever met her or portrayed her in your games as a storyteller? If so, how do you portray her? The name implies she was possibly a prophetess, but not much is provided about her true nature and purposes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T10:00:00-07:00","id":1508365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508356-have-you-ever-portrayed-sybil-in-your-games#post1508356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello everyone, I'd like to discuss something here regarding Sybil. We've never had much information about her, save that she's the only &quot;known&quot; female embraced by the &quot;father of the Abyss&quot; (i.e. The Lasombra Antediluvian). Have you ever met her or portrayed her in your games as a storyteller? If so, how do you portray her? The name implies she was possibly a prophetess, but not much is provided about her true nature and purposes.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Supposing</i> that neither Sejanus nor her ever commited diablerie, that is. Remember that for many years <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Anne_Bowesley\" target=\"_blank\">Lady Anne</a> was &quot;known&quot; to be 6th generation, with the logical implication about her sire Valerius' own lineage. <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Valerius\" target=\"_blank\">Except not</a>.<br /> <br /> Things are not exactly what they can seem at first brush. Narrators can be unreliable, especially among the kindred. Remember <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Veddartha\" target=\"_blank\">the matter of Veddartha</a>.<br /> <br /> <br /> But yeah, speaking of the figure per se, i tend to stick to &quot;mirrors, smoke &amp; shadows&quot; theory - Sybil is a cypher, possibly of Vitel's fabrication in considerable part, let's remember the man is a master of Obfuscate that dedicated <b>at least one elder power</b> <i>to making the matter of his identity/lineage confusing and untraceable</i>.<br /> <br /> Do we even know he's in truth Sejanus? Because that <b>also</b> being a lie would definitely explain <b>a lot</b> of discrepancies between his background/fluff and the historical figure....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-14-2023, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T10:51:47-07:00","id":1508368,"title":"","content":"I got a notification that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1147_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1147\" data-vbnamecard=\"1147\">Baaldam</a> commented, but I can't see his comment. I really don't get it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T11:23:26-07:00","id":1508372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508356-have-you-ever-portrayed-sybil-in-your-games?p=1508368#post1508368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got a notification that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1147_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1147\" data-vbnamecard=\"1147\">Baaldam</a> commented, but I can't see his comment. I really don't get it.</div> </div> </div> </div>System nonsense - my message got suspected of being spam because i edited it twice in a few minutes or whatever. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> But anyway, my point is that Masquerade is a setting of unreliable narrators per excellence. Vitel is 5th gen, ergo his sire is a 4th gen and the <b><i>extra mysterious</i></b> rogue/secret/apocryphal childe of the Lasombra Antediluvian.... but is she really?<br /> <br /> - Helena (from Chicago by Night) is 4th gen, but by virtue of diablerizing her side Minos - but how many kindred actually know that and instead think incorrectly that she is a childe of Arikel (or whatever is the true name of the Toreador clan founder)?<br /> - Lady Anne was &quot;known&quot; to be 6th gen for about half a decade until Giovanni Chronicles II &amp; III revealed her as actually a 8th gen and serial diablerist.<br /> - Vitel/Sejanus' highest elder power is an Obfuscate one, related <i>to masking his lineage/identity</i>.<br /> <br /> So, there's a lot of room in their history for the facts to be more convoluted than BJD's hooks imply.<br /> <br /> Maybe Sybil diablerized her way to 4th gen sometime before Sejanus was even born.<br /> Or maybe she was of weaker blood and he raised himself to 5th in his almost 2 millenia of unlife.<br /> Is &quot;Vitel's&quot; shadowy pupetter really his sire or just someone toying with his unawareness?<br /> <br /> Plus, the prince was <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Art_Morgan\" target=\"_blank\">not the only methuselah</a> hiding in plain sight amidst DC's nocturnal society. <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Bjorn_Garinson\" target=\"_blank\">Far from it</a>, in fact.<br /> Why is no one speaking of <b>their </b>sires? Because <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Xaviar\" target=\"_blank\">maybe we should</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-14-2023, 02:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T12:59:34-07:00","id":1508379,"title":"","content":"Welcome to the magic world of spam traps. It wiil be approved eventually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T22:21:18-07:00","id":1508417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508356-have-you-ever-portrayed-sybil-in-your-games?p=1508379#post1508379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Welcome to the magic world of spam traps. It wiil be approved eventually.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the second time it happened this week. In any case, it seems nobody ever used her in their stories. I've always wondered how much aware was Marcus Vitel of her influence in his actions and how he felt about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T09:44:51-07:00","id":1508456,"title":"","content":"I think something along the lines of Critias Herr Meister.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T17:27:50-07:00","id":1508496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508356-have-you-ever-portrayed-sybil-in-your-games?p=1508456#post1508456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think something along the lines of Critias Herr Meister.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even though both characters are absolutely different. I mean, Marcus Vitel is a &quot;grand manipulator&quot; and schemer, it must feel very strange for him if he's aware he's just a piece in someone's else table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T20:36:07-07:00","id":1508508,"title":"","content":"I've used her as a background character in a couple of games who was working as a secret patron for the player characters, or the secret patron of their secret patron. In life she was a prophetess, and it's believed that she was Embraced somewhere in South or Central America 3000 to 4000 years ago. After becoming a vampire she became obsessed with the Abyss, spending a great deal of time there and is currently the foremost master of Abyss Mysticism in existence. She is also the only Lasombra that is (ostensibly) still loyal to Lasombra - she helped him with his plan to become one with the Abyss and continues to serve as his hands in the real world, moving between the Abyss and Earth.<br /> <br /> Sybil is technically a member of the Lasombra Antitribu purely due to the fact that she did not join the Sabbat. The Sabbat have attempted to kill her a few times over the centuries, but those assassination attempts were unsuccessful (the last of which was spectacularly so). Still, she doesn't appear to oppose the Sabbat or carry a grudge (and has contacts with some of the elder Lasombra within the faction and has even assisted them on a few occasions) so they have mostly ended up adopting an &quot;unlive-and-let-unlive&quot; policy with her. She also maintains contact with Montano and some of the other elder Lasombra Antitribu. None of them have any idea that Lasombra still exists or that she's still working for him.<br /> <br /> In the Modern Nights, she's mostly a forgotten and apocryphal individual, and only a small number of Lasombra have ever heard of her, and even fewer know that she still exists. She's very much a puppet master, who hides in the Abyss, using her powers of foresight to push other vampires into certain courses of action to conform with the future that she's seen. She professes her loyalty to Lasombra, but Lasombra has begun to doubt that. At the same time, he also can't do anything because she's irreplaceable to him and his plans. He can't sire any new childer and it would take centuries for any else to approach her mastery over the Abyss. He's in the uncomfortable position of being almost entirely dependent on her, but also not being able to trust her either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T22:01:55-07:00","id":1508510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but those assassination attempts were unsuccessful (the last of which was spectacularly so </div> </div> </div>Would you care to elaborate on that? You got me curious there hahaha.<br /> <br /> The way you used her is very interesting, although, given her name I made her Greek in my game, but she's also a prophetess and has been one since her mortal days. So, in your game her Mastery of Abyss Mysticism is even greater than Montano's? I wish we had character sheets for Cainites like Montano and more information on her from the official books. Still, as I said, I'm very interested in hearing (reading) more about her actions in your game and particularly the accounts of this spectacularly unsuccessful attempt on her unlife.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T00:14:51-07:00","id":1508515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508356-have-you-ever-portrayed-sybil-in-your-games?p=1508510#post1508510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would you care to elaborate on that? You got me curious there hahaha.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically a Sabbat vampire diablarized her, or thought they diablarized her, but they actually just swallowed an Abyss monster (either it was perfectly disguised as her or she had placed it into her blood). It began tearing her assailant apart from the inside out and then puppeted his still-screaming head on abyssal spider legs into the sunlight where both vampire and Abyss demon vanished. It was a gruesome enough demise that the Sabbat mostly got the message and decided to just stop going after her.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508356-have-you-ever-portrayed-sybil-in-your-games?p=1508510#post1508510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way you used her is very interesting, although, given her name I made her Greek in my game, but she's also a prophetess and has been one since her mortal days.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have her as a member of a group that was a precursor to the Olmecs. She was a seer and ended up spending much of her mortal life confined in an underground cave. Lasombra felt a strange draw to her and was impressed with her ability to see the future. After her embrace she followed him as an advisor. Eventually they ended up in Greece where she adopted the name/title of Sybil.<br /> <br /> She was a priestess of a now forgotten god of darkness and believes her visions of the future still come from that being (or some being, her religious beliefs have shifted a bit over several thousand years and she largely belives that many different gods are one being and that being is still giving her visions). She believes that it's her duty to see to it that those visions of the future come to pass.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508356-have-you-ever-portrayed-sybil-in-your-games?p=1508510#post1508510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in your game her Mastery of Abyss Mysticism is even greater than Montano's? I wish we had character sheets for Cainites like Montano and more information on her from the official books. Still, as I said, I'm very interested in hearing (reading) more about her actions in your game and particularly the accounts of this spectacularly unsuccessful attempt on her unlife.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never fully statted her because I've never directly used her in a game, just more indirectly. I'd probably put the majority of her experience into Obteneration and ton of unique Abyss Rituals. She'd have high Auspex, maybe 5 dots in Dominate and Potence, but not much else. She'd very much be a &quot;one trick pony&quot; where she'd be better than Montano at Abyss Mysticism but he'd be better than her at most everything else.<br /> <br /> As for her relationship with her own Childer she mostly has a hands-off policy. She only embraces when she has a vision of her embracing someone, and then she assumes that there must be a reason for that. She she gives them some basic level of training but mostly leaves them to their own devices after that. The god that gives her visions must have some plan for her childe, and if she doesn't receive any visions as to what it is, then it must not be her business <br /> <br /> One of the only times I used her in a campaign was in a gonzo crossover game. One of the players was playing a Lasombra antitribu and was focusing on Abyss Mysticism, and she was serving as his mentor. The players were trying to get their hands on the Antichrist Serum (from Book of the Weaver). Sybil was also trying to get it, as it was the last necessary thing to complete Lasombra's apotheosis. The serum ended up getting stolen by a group of Angellis Ater who were in league with a group of Nephandi and wanted to use it to summon up the horrible monster they believed it was linked to.<br /> <br /> Sybil didn't get directly involved. She sent some of her agents to help and gave the Lasombra PC an artifact to amplify his powers and in exchange he was supposed to give her the serum when it was recovered. But during the climax it ended up falling into a volcano and the PCs weren't going to rush in after it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 04-16-2023, 03:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T02:21:19-07:00","id":1508520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Basically a Sabbat vampire diablarized her, or thought they diablarized her, but they actually just swallowed an Abyss monster (either it was perfectly disguised as her or she had placed it into her blood). It began tearing her assailant apart from the inside out and then puppeted his still-screaming head on abyssal spider legs into the sunlight where both vampire and Abyss demon vanished. It was a gruesome enough demise that the Sabbat mostly got the message and decided to just stop going after her. </div> </div> </div>Hahaha that was very cool. I really liked that, I would even like it more if it was one of the PCs in my games hahaha (yes, sometimes I have these &quot;evil temptations as an ST).<br /> <br /> I like to give stats to every important NPC in my games, but I understand that it saves a lot of time not doing it, besides the fact that many times it's a complete waste of time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> have her as a member of a group that was a precursor to the Olmecs. She was a seer and ended up spending much of her mortal life confined in an underground cave. Lasombra felt a strange draw to her and was impressed with her ability to see the future. After her embrace she followed him as an advisor. Eventually they ended up in Greece where she adopted the name/title of Sybil.<br /> <br /> She was a priestess of a now forgotten god of darkness and believes her visions of the future still come from that being (or some being, her religious beliefs have shifted a bit over several thousand years and she largely belives that many different gods are one being and that being is still giving her visions). She believes that it's her duty to see to it that those visions of the future come to pass.\u200b </div> </div> </div>This character development was also very interesting, I still haven't thought much about her relationship with &quot;The Father of the Abyss&quot;, but I focused more in her relationship with Marcus Vitel as he's the patron of my PCs at the moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T10:57:49-07:00","id":1508541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508356-have-you-ever-portrayed-sybil-in-your-games?p=1508496#post1508496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even though both characters are absolutely different. I mean, Marcus Vitel is a &quot;grand manipulator&quot; and schemer, it must feel very strange for him if he's aware he's just a piece in someone's else table.</div> </div> </div> </div>I bet it would be a strange experience for Vitel and be somewhat humbling to go up against someone more skilled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T15:09:14-07:00","id":1508569,"title":"","content":"No. I tend not to use any childer of the antedeluvians in the chronicles I ST. Even when I use ancient Methusalehs of potent blood as responsible for something (usually in torpor), I stick to the fifth generation vampires who never met their sire's sire.<br /> <br /> I also have an internal rule on Lasombra lineages based on the idea originally discussed in Montano's chapter of Kindred of the Revolution - except for Montano, Lasombra eventually destroys all his childer because they always disappoint him for not being loyal enough. Such childer might live for centuries or even thousands of years and have various childer of their own, but he eventually destroys them. Montano is the only exception.<br /> <br /> So I would have the Sybil be a childe Laosmbra created after he embraced Montano. Just so she can exist in order to embrace Sejanus. But she was destroyed herself before Lasombra embraced Gratiano. She might have been the only childe created by Lasombra inbetween Montano and Gratiano. It is precisely this history of Lasombra destroying his childer that prompted Gratiano to join the Anarch Revolts - he didn't want to eventually end up on the menu.<br /> <br /> I just think the &quot;story&quot; between Montano and Gratiano works better, if they are only surviving &quot;siblings&quot;.<br /> <br /> Another possibility is that Sybil still exists and is 4th generation, but isn't the childe of Lasombra. Instead she diablerized her way to 4th generation (perhaps devouring another childe of Lasombra with his approval, or another clan). I'd have to use this if I wanted Sybil to still be around and somehow manipulating Vitel and others in the DC area. But if I remember correctly, while we are given hints that the Sybil was involved in both Vitel and Marissa, I don't think we actually got any details of her plans like we did with Helena and Menele in Chicago. So I think it'd be very easy to run a DC chronicle and not utilize Sybil as a real background presence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T17:03:18-07:00","id":1508586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think we actually got any details of her plans like we did with Helena and Menele in Chicago. So I think it'd be very easy to run a DC chronicle and not utilize Sybil as a real background presence. </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's &quot;my problem&quot; actually, the thing is we don't have much information about her and so we must come up with our own. I was curious about how other STs have used her in their games. Your take is interesting, regarding the children of Lasombra, but I think there could be many other reasons for Gratiano to want to topple his sire, ambition is the easierst of them all, especially because Gratiano was known to be a very ambitious Cainite. Just for the sake of curiosity, do you think the diablerie on Lasombra really worked? Isn't it TOO strange that Gratiano is a nrealy forgotten figure in the Sabbat, even after the deed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T17:39:42-07:00","id":1508589,"title":"","content":"In regards to Grantino I don\u2019t think he successfully diablerized his sire at all and going by the Lasombra clan trilogy he was subjected to high levels of Dominate and kept messing up the final deaths of Lasombra and Tzismce.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T17:43:55-07:00","id":1508590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508356-have-you-ever-portrayed-sybil-in-your-games?p=1508589#post1508589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In regards to Grantino I don\u2019t think he successfully diablerized his sire at all and going by the Lasombra clan trilogy he was subjected to high levels of Dominate and kept messing up the final deaths of Lasombra and Tzismce.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with it, I used to joke that I thought Lasombra faking his destruction was so successful that even most players thought he was really destroyed, but these same players used to agree that Tzimisce survived the attempt hahaha...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T17:47:53-07:00","id":1508591,"title":"","content":"Yeah I think his sire saw him as a great puppet to use to further his own interests and not be bothered by lesser vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T17:55:48-07:00","id":1508593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508356-have-you-ever-portrayed-sybil-in-your-games?p=1508591#post1508591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I think his sire saw him as a great puppet to use to further his own interests and not be bothered by lesser vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, also if one thinks of the possible plots Lasombra had, he certainly was able to get many options to influence both Camarilla and the Sabbat, as he possibly has not only Gratiano, but also possibly Sybil and Vitel, these two that had huge amounts of influence in the Camarilla and some in the Sabbat as well. There are indeed many options to explore regarding his plans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T18:02:22-07:00","id":1508594,"title":"","content":"Your onto something Herr Meister and Montano seemed to been conditioned during the revolt from some lore suggesting that he couldn\u2019t truly recall any details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T19:12:13-07:00","id":1508597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508356-have-you-ever-portrayed-sybil-in-your-games?p=1508594#post1508594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your onto something Herr Meister and Montano seemed to been conditioned during the revolt from some lore suggesting that he couldn\u2019t truly recall any details.</div> </div> </div> </div>By the way, you reminded me of something I've always wondered. What was Montano doing all this time since the Anarch Revolt? Some say he suppedly got a seat in the Camarilla's Inner Circle or that he had some kind of protection, but nothing is really clear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T22:36:25-07:00","id":1508606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508356-have-you-ever-portrayed-sybil-in-your-games?p=1508586#post1508586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just for the sake of curiosity, do you think the diablerie on Lasombra really worked? Isn't it TOO strange that Gratiano is a nrealy forgotten figure in the Sabbat, even after the deed?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't run Sabbat games, so that's not really an important question for me to answer. But in a general perspective, I view the Sabbat as a horribly compromised organization that is a poor, degraded corruption of the original Anarchs so my ideas on the diablerie of Lasombra follow that general idea. Gratiano and his co-conspirators only found an empty tomb. There was no diablerie or destruction of Lasombra. They merely claimed to have destroyed him - possibly a result of Domination screwing with their memory.<br /> <br /> In my chronicle setting, some of the Lasombra anti-tribu believe that Gratiano's plot with the Anarchs was really a plot by Lasombra to see who in his clan were really loyal to him. (We must remember that originally the Lasombra clan was one of the hardest enemies of the Anarchs prior to Gratiano's attack.) Lasombra embraced Gratiano for the explicit purpose to &quot;test&quot; the entire clan. He knew what Gratiano was ultimately going to do. He wanted to see what would happen if his clan thought he was destroyed. Gratiano was his tool to do so. Now he does. So these anti-tribu believe Lasombra is alive and is going to wipe out his entire clan (except for them) once Gehenna arrives. Not all Lasombra anti-tribu believe this, but a substantial minority of them do. Are they right? Who knows? Montano cannot give his opinions because he has been in torpor for the last several centuries.<br /> <br /> Gratiano isn't a complete non-entity in the Sabbat, but he obviously is not in a leadership role that he &quot;should&quot; be in given his deeds. (At least Lugoj Bloodbreaker isn't a leader because it is known &quot;he&quot; went into torpor soon thereafter.) Why isn't he? It isn't because of some principle - Gratiano was always an opportunistic shit who sought power. It is because he is not actually good at being a leader or politician. He has some talents of course - good enough to be Archbishop somewhere and claims he isn't more because of some principle. In reality it is because he just isn't great enough to survive the politics of the Regent, Cardinals, and Consistory. This really confuses a lot of Sabbat. A lot of Sabbat project their ideals upon Gratiano and believe everything wrong with the sect would be made &quot;right&quot; if he were Regent. Gratiano uses this support when convenient, but knows if he actually tried to lead the sect it'd blow up in his face. He just isn't as good as a plotter as many other in the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> I do not claim this was &quot;canon&quot;. It is just the interpretation I like best for my own chronicles.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T22:44:44-07:00","id":1508607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508356-have-you-ever-portrayed-sybil-in-your-games?p=1508597#post1508597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, you reminded me of something I've always wondered. What was Montano doing all this time since the Anarch Revolt? Some say he suppedly got a seat in the Camarilla's Inner Circle or that he had some kind of protection, but nothing is really clear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Montano should be incredibly ancient. I dislike the idea that he is active as a result. In my setting, he was actually quite active in Camarilla politics early on. If he had stayed awake, he might have even rallied enough of his clan to join the Camarilla and have a seat on the Inner Circle. (One of my setting ideas is that a great number of Lasombra hesitated to join the Camarilla but were not originally Anarch, but eventually decided on the Sabbat as something they could &quot;control&quot; once the post-Thorns Anarchs became organized enough to become Sabbat.) But he entered torpor relatively soon after (&quot;soon&quot; might mean one or even two centuries), and there was no other Lasombra anti-tribu of his credibility and authority to take his place, so they were never able to be any political equal to the traditional seven clans.<br /> <br /> I think Montano being awake and active leads to too many questions that cannot be adequately answered. So torpor was my best solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T22:47:24-07:00","id":1508608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508356-have-you-ever-portrayed-sybil-in-your-games?p=1508606#post1508606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't run Sabbat games, so that's not really an important question for me to answer. But in a general perspective, I view the Sabbat as a horribly compromised organization that is a poor, degraded corruption of the original Anarchs so my ideas on the diablerie of Lasombra follow that general idea. Gratiano and his co-conspirators only found an empty tomb. There was no diablerie or destruction of Lasombra. They merely claimed to have destroyed him - possibly a result of Domination screwing with their memory.<br /> <br /> In my chronicle setting, some of the Lasombra anti-tribu believe that Gratiano's plot with the Anarchs was really a plot by Lasombra to see who in his clan were really loyal to him. (We must remember that originally the Lasombra clan was one of the hardest enemies of the Anarchs prior to Gratiano's attack.) Lasombra embraced Gratiano for the explicit purpose to &quot;test&quot; the entire clan. He knew what Gratiano was ultimately going to do. He wanted to see what would happen if his clan thought he was destroyed. Gratiano was his tool to do so. Now he does. So these anti-tribu believe Lasombra is alive and is going to wipe out his entire clan (except for them) once Gehenna arrives. Not all Lasombra anti-tribu believe this, but a substantial minority of them do. Are they right? Who knows? Montano cannot give his opinions because he has been in torpor for the last several centuries.<br /> <br /> Gratiano isn't a complete non-entity in the Sabbat, but he obviously is not in a leadership role that he &quot;should&quot; be in given his deeds. (At least Lugoj Bloodbreaker isn't a leader because it is known &quot;he&quot; went into torpor soon thereafter.) Why isn't he? It isn't because of some principle - Gratiano was always an opportunistic shit who sought power. It is because he is not actually good at being a leader or politician. He has some talents of course - good enough to be Archbishop somewhere and claims he isn't more because of some principle. In reality it is because he just isn't great enough to survive the politics of the Regent, Cardinals, and Consistory. This really confuses a lot of Sabbat. A lot of Sabbat project their ideals upon Gratiano and believe everything wrong with the sect would be made &quot;right&quot; if he were Regent. Gratiano uses this support when convenient, but knows if he actually tried to lead the sect it'd blow up in his face. He just isn't as good as a plotter as many other in the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> I do not claim this was &quot;canon&quot;. It is just the interpretation I like best for my own chronicles.</div> </div> </div> </div>In general, I like your interpretation of the facts. But I still believe Gratiano got satisfied with too little, given his blood and his &quot;supposed deed&quot;. Even if he wasn't really that talented for politics, for starters, being 4th generation does help a lot in many regards, especially when there's a legend surrounding you. About the regency in the Sabbat, I find it really weird that Melinda Galbraith of all Cainites got to become Regent. She's a diabolist and the Sabbat stance against infernalism is quite clear, still she seemed to suffer no consequences for that.<br /> <br /> I like the idea that some of Lasombra's descendants are still loyal to him and act as if he would spare them in the event of Gehenna, that reminds me of the <i>Manus Nigrum</i> aka Tal'Mahe'Ra. If I'm not mistaken in Becket's Diary there's a theory that what people think is Marcus Vitel could be the Antediluvian Lasombra himself, but I find it weird, why would a creature of such a power &quot;be in the open&quot; in such a busy position as Vitel's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T00:32:45-07:00","id":1508616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508356-have-you-ever-portrayed-sybil-in-your-games?p=1508608#post1508608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> About the regency in the Sabbat, I find it really weird that Melinda Galbraith of all Cainites got to become Regent. She's a diabolist and the Sabbat stance against infernalism is quite clear, still she seemed to suffer no consequences for that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bIn my 1991 game Melinda Galbraith is the Regent but pretends to be Patricia of Bollingbroke, who is &quot;incognito&quot; as Tyler in Chicago. She was able to trick most people who has met her because they use to be packmates in Spain during the Anarch revolt and fled together to Mexico. When a lot of Sabbat neonates arrived there she took advantage and claimed a Bishopric a later a Cardinal seat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T03:53:33-07:00","id":1508625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508356-have-you-ever-portrayed-sybil-in-your-games?p=1508616#post1508616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bIn my 1991 game Melinda Galbraith is the Regent but pretends to be Patricia of Bollingbroke, who is &quot;incognito&quot; as Tyler in Chicago. She was able to trick most people who has met her because they use to be packmates in Spain during the Anarch revolt and fled together to Mexico. When a lot of Sabbat neonates arrived there she took advantage and claimed a Bishopric a later a Cardinal seat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very interesting take on Galbraith and Bollingbroke as well. I suppose she's not an infernalist in your game, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T08:55:22-07:00","id":1508754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508356-have-you-ever-portrayed-sybil-in-your-games?p=1508586#post1508586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, that's &quot;my problem&quot; actually, the thing is we don't have much information about her and so we must come up with our own. I was curious about how other STs have used her in their games. Your take is interesting, regarding the children of Lasombra, but I think there could be many other reasons for Gratiano to want to topple his sire, ambition is the easierst of them all, especially because Gratiano was known to be a very ambitious Cainite. Just for the sake of curiosity, do you think the diablerie on Lasombra really worked? Isn't it TOO strange that Gratiano is a nrealy forgotten figure in the Sabbat, even after the deed?</div> </div> </div> </div>As you can probably guess from my previous posts - supposing they are visible now hopefully - i tend to be somewhat contrarian with the idea of Sybil, but then i'm not a fan of characters of assumed greatness by virtue of being the sire or childe of a fan favorite as a whole. Combined with the fact Vitel/Sejanus is <i>pretty much built up around the idea of being a monster at falsifying his identity</i> and well...<br /> <br /> <br /> The one time she did appear in my games she was found in torpor in one of departed Prince Marissa's &quot;abandoned&quot; havens, 6th generation and macguffin to reveal that everything the PCs - or their allies, the Black sisters - thought they knew about DC's prince was either wrong or purposefully false. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-18-2023, 11:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T09:07:08-07:00","id":1508758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508356-have-you-ever-portrayed-sybil-in-your-games?p=1508625#post1508625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Very interesting take on Galbraith and Bollingbroke as well. I suppose she's not an infernalist in your game, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not really relevant as she is just a background character. I decided to do the switch because the game is set in Chicago and the real Patricia of Bollingbroke is there incognito, so I wanted to throw a fake clue when the characters were doing some background research about the Sabbat","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}